      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original informed by its own earlier source preparation; the independent current English original has not been read. Original forms, intermediate forms and observers keep their separate occurrences despite English reversals. The second distance phrase is retained at phrase depth, while the final far qualifier is provisionally proposed as at a distance and requires skeptical review. The complete arising-aspect expression is retained as impression; clear stays unwrapped despite the positive rnam pa glossary variant. The appearance clarity adverbs belong to their own clauses. Repeated gsal, snang and the negative-question bsgribs have no separately printed exponent because English shares their positive predicate across or not; these are ellipsis nulls, not uncertainty labels. The sole Tibetan name and Numerist assertion own one English occurrence each. Intermediate, original, object participants, whether-or-not scaffolding, skye ba existence/result expansion, yin gyi contrast and redundant pronouns are omitted where distributed or supplied. Source wording and hgm_gloss remain unchanged; reconciliation and semantic review are still required."
